## Lore

Sales Representatives are the Northern Gun employees most customers meet. Unlike a modern customer-service job, an NG Sales Rep accompanies shipments on perilous journeys and sells to the most dangerous and unpredictable clients. They staff every official Northern Gun outlet and handle special orders and deliveries to remote locations. Because Northern Gun is above all an arms dealer, a Sales Rep knows how its weapons, combat vehicles, robots and power armor work and is good with a gun; most worked their way up from lower sales jobs or the maintenance or security divisions, and can call for backup from the IMCN or the Loss Prevention Office.

City Sales Reps are often technical specialists with a natural knack for closing a sale. Wilderness or "field" Sales Reps, and those stationed in Escanaba or Menominee, add languages and familiarity with mercenaries and tribal peoples. All are trained to be discreet and to sell to anyone, including secret shipments to non-humans, practitioners of magic, pirates, criminals and Black Marketeers.

Alignment: Any, but most are Scrupulous, Unprincipled and Anarchist. The higher the M.E. and M.A. the better. All official Sales Reps in Ishpeming are human; out in the field, 15% are D-Bees.

## Equipment

NG light M.D.C. body armor, NG energy pistol of choice, 4 spare E-Clips, pocket computer, personal radio (10 mile/16 km range), Northern Gun sales uniform, traveling clothes, hiking boots, backpack, knapsack, binoculars, waterproof lighter and 1D4x10 copies of the Northern Gun catalog.

Wilderness Sales Reps most likely have a personal vehicle such as a motorcycle, hovertruck or hovercycle; some use riding animals better suited to the terrain.

## Pay and cybernetics

Pay is 4,000 NGMI credits a month; characters start with one month''s pay.

None to start. Some Sales Reps have computers or communication devices installed to help with the job, and many acquire minor helpful and cosmetic cybernetics over time.
